          "text": "请看到这篇帖子的人，去给马来西亚大学发邮件（integrity@um.edu.my），为最近墙内热搜上遭遇大规模incel网暴的被摸臀的女性澄清辩护。\n\n(或者直接去@unimalaya 的官号下面留言或者私信）\n\n标题一定要鲜明：就是为该女生辩护\n\n核心就一条：要让校方意识到，这是一场由官方发起的，煽动极右翼厌女狂欢的文化战争和猎巫运动，并非单纯的普通社会事件。\n\n英联邦系高校对于学生的处理问题必须遵循程序正义原则。而incel们给校方贯垃圾邮件，网暴开盒等等行为早就已经造成不可逆转的偏见，校方几乎不可能以客观中立的方式调查此事，已经严重损害了正当程序。\n\n同时，一定要强调，很多中国用户举报信里提到的内容，如“锁喉”，“女方诬告”都存在严重夸大，目前并没有任何司法证据支撑。\n\n我这条并不怕被incel网暴。\n\n因为incel越给我推流，这条就能让更多的人看到。看到的人数量多了，声援女方的邮件也会越多。\n\n下面这个是我写的，可以参考一下：\n\nDear Officer at the University of Malaya,\n\nI am writing to defend Ms. Jinting Chen, who is at the centre of a recent pile-on from Chinese users regarding her alleged misconduct, and to explain how a minor social incident was turned into a witch-hunt against women by state-owned media and state-sponsored radical nationalists.\n\nThe first point I would like to make is that the reports from these Chinese users contain significant exaggeration and misinformation. There has never been any formal account stating that Ms. Chen ever \"strangled the child\" or committed \"alleged sexual misconduct against a child.\" All existing evidence solely indicates that she confronted the child's parents and requested an apology after their child touched her buttocks.\n\nSecondly, the reporting itself is highly coordinated and purpose-built, rather than factual and neutral. The accounts piling on with reports on social media (mainly on X) belong primarily to radical nationalists and anti-feminists. Some even call themselves \"Zhiminists\" to show their respect for Dong Zhimin, the convicted rapist and human trafficker from Fengxian, Xuzhou, Jiangsu Province. Their actions happen to align with state propaganda aimed at increasing the birth rate, weaponizing a minor behavioral dispute to crack down on feminism.\n\nI hope the University of Malaya will investigate this matter impartially, without being influenced by publicity that is highly directional and politically driven. In light of the divided opinions currently on social media, making a temporary accommodation to a one-sided narrative may not be the most ideal approach in the long term.\n\nKind regards,"
        },
